{"issue": 90, "stage": "reply", "reply_id": "IC_kwDORdtOLc8AAAABeiYktQ", "author": "MikeEchoVoid", "created": "2026-10-22T15:17:03Z", "excerpt": "Confirmed fixed on 1.8.13. A project document under `docs/reports/` opened through `/file/` now shows its `# title` once (one `<h1>`), and the \"View in Fabric\" link is gone for a file without a component card. Thank you.\n", "answered": false, "ts": "2026-10-22T20:17:05Z"}
{"issue": 92, "stage": "reply", "reply_id": "IC_kwDORdtOLc8AAAABekVrTg", "author": "MikeEchoVoid", "created": "2026-10-22T16:55:09Z", "excerpt": "Thank you for building this so quickly.\n\nIn our setup the \"Awaiting review\" column stays empty on purpose: a task only enters it with a verdict from the independent AI reviewer, and we chose not to enable one (reviews of our deliverables stay human-only). So I cannot confirm the column from real use.\n\nWhat we actually needed, as in the original request, is to see the tasks where the agent is done and the human has to act. Today we get that from `owner: human` and the `/tasks?owner=human` view, w", "answered": false, "ts": "2026-10-22T20:17:05Z"}
{"issue": 93, "stage": "reply", "reply_id": "IC_kwDORdtOLc8AAAABeiZKVQ", "author": "MikeEchoVoid", "created": "2026-10-22T15:17:27Z", "excerpt": "Looks fixed on 1.8.13, checked on the rendered page only. On `/inception/T-002` of a freshly initialised project, the unticked Human criterion is rendered as a checkbox in a form posting to `/api/task/T-002/toggle-ac`, and the page header links to the task page. I have not clicked it in a browser, as there is no unticked inception criterion in the project where I work. Thank you.\n", "answered": false, "ts": "2026-10-22T20:17:05Z"}
{"issue": 94, "stage": "reply", "reply_id": "IC_kwDORdtOLc8AAAABeiZvDg", "author": "MikeEchoVoid", "created": "2026-10-22T15:17:49Z", "excerpt": "Confirmed fixed on 1.8.13. On the inception page of a task made from the stock template, the Verification card now shows the section verbatim in a `<pre>` block, `#` comment lines included, instead of turning them into headings. Thank you.\n", "answered": false, "ts": "2026-10-22T20:17:05Z"}
